IMPORTANT — GPL-3.0 IN DISTRIBUTED BINARIES
================================================================================

The Apache-2.0 licence above covers the source code in this repository. It does
NOT cover the native libraries this project links against at build time, and one
of them carries stronger obligations.

sherpa-onnx ships a single native library, libsherpa-onnx-jni.so, which has
espeak-ng statically compiled into it. espeak-ng is licensed GPL-3.0.

Verified in sherpa-onnx 1.13.4, jni/arm64-v8a/libsherpa-onnx-jni.so:
  - espeak-ng data-file names: phondata, phontab, phonindex, intonations
  - espeak-ng runtime strings: ESPEAK_DATA_PATH, "/usr/share/espeak-ng-data",
    "Failed to initialize espeak-ng with data dir"
  - a literal espeak-ng source string: "Could not load the mbrola.dll file"

Consequences for anyone shipping an application built on this SDK:

  1. The obligation attaches to distributing the linked binary, not to whether
     espeak-ng is called. Choosing a text-to-speech model that never invokes it
     does not avoid this: Kokoro, Piper, Kitten and Matcha all live in the same
     library.

  2. An application that distributes libsherpa-onnx-jni.so is distributing
     GPL-3.0 code and must satisfy GPL-3.0 for the combined work, including
     making the corresponding source available.

  3. Avoiding this requires rebuilding sherpa-onnx with
     -DSHERPA_ONNX_ENABLE_TTS=OFF, which removes espeak-ng and all text-to-speech
     with it, and supplying a replacement grapheme-to-phoneme stage under a
     permissive licence.

This is a summary of technical findings, not legal advice. See issue #27.


